#+ Intro test scenario
#@{
#### Intro common
	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_intro_title"
	val[]: "Truck Driving Basics"

	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_intro_desc"
	val[]: "Replay the introduction cutscene"
#@}

#+ Book 1 Scenario 1_01
#@{

#### 1_01 common
	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_01_title"
	val[]: "Before You Drive"

	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_01_desc"
	val[]: "For your first scenario, we'll go through the basics of the driver's cabin. It's important to correctly adjust your seat, steering wheel and side mirrors, as having proper visibility is important for managing stressful or precarious situations.<br><br>We'll go over the controls for adjusting these components one at a time."

#### 1_01 goal

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_01_adjuster"
	val[]: "Seat and Mirror Adjustment"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_01_check_adj"
	val[]: "Mirror and Visibility Check"

#### 1_01 msg - intro text

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_01_cutscene1"
	val[]: "Welcome to your first lesson!<br>Let's start by learning how to prepare the truck to hit the road."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_01_cutscene2"
	val[]: "It is crucial to ensure that your driving is safe, professional and under control at all times.<br>The proper adjustment of the seat, steering wheel and mirrors will help you to accomplish this."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_01_cutscene3"
	val[]: "On each side of the truck, there are some vehicles.<br>They'll help guide you to adjust the mirrors properly."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_01_cutscene4"
	val[]: "Take your time to adjust everything to your liking as these settings<br>will have a significant impact on your ability to control the truck."

#### 1_01 Driving Instructions

	key[]: "adj_tut_title_0"
	val[]: "Seat and Steering Wheel Adjustment"

	key[]: "adj_tut_title_1"
	val[]: "Adjusting Main Mirrors"

	key[]: "adj_tut_title_2"
	val[]: "Adjusting Convex Mirrors"

	key[]: "adj_tut_title_3"
	val[]: "Visibility Check and Final Mirror Adjustment"

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_adj_keyboard"
	val[]: "press @@imv_nrm_adjuster@@ or access it through vehicle adjustments in the pause menu"

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_adj_gamepad"
	val[]: "access it through the vehicle adjustments in the pause menu"

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_adj"
	val[]: "To display '@@adjust_link_t@@' during gameplay, $OPEN_ADJUSTER$."

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_seat"
	val[]: "First, let's adjust the driver's seat and steering wheel.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Open '@@adj_seats@@' to continue.</font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_mirrors"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Open @@adj_mirrors@@ to configure the mirror settings.</font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_adj_intro"
	val[]: "When getting into a truck for the first time, it's important to first adjust the seat, steering wheel and mirrors to your liking.<br><br>The correct position behind the steering wheel is crucial for proper visibility. All controls must be within reach, and the driver needs to have a clear view ahead, to the sides, and in the mirrors.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>To display the configuration menu, $OPEN_ADJUSTER$. </font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_seat_and_back_adj"
	val[]: "@@adj_tut_set_seat_and_back_adj_img@@<br>Adjust the seat so that you have a clear view of your surroundings as well as the mirrors, and so that you can reach all controls.<br><br>Adjust the steering wheel so that it is in a comfortable position and doesn't block your view of any instruments.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>When you are satisfied with your adjustments, press @@imv_nrm_back@@ to return to the configuration menu. </font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_mirrors_intro"
	val[]: "@@adj_tut_open_mirrors_intro_img@@<br>Trucks have many large blind spots, so they are equipped with multiple exterior mirrors to help the driver see as much as possible. <br><br>Proper adjustment of these mirrors will allow you to have the best possible visibility of your surroundings.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Open '@@adj_mirrors@@' to continue.</font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_1_adj"
	val[]: "@@adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_1_adj_img@@<br>The main mirrors cover the space along the side of the truck and trailer.<br><br>To adjust the correct position of the main mirrors, use the cars on both sides of the vehicle for reference.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_selectfcs@@ to continue.</font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_2_adj"
	val[]: "The main mirrors are your primary tool for seeing what is going on beside and behind you. You should have a good view of the car beside you, but make sure to keep some of the trailer in the mirror as well to help you accurately judge the position of obstacles around you."

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_2_adj_big"
	val[]: "Once you are satisfied with the adjustment, switch to the passenger's side main mirror."

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_2_adj_moved"
	val[]: "Again, you should have a good view of the car beside you while keeping some of the trailer visible in the mirror too."

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_2_adj_moved_big"
	val[]: "Once you are satisfied with the mirror adjustment, switch to the driver's side convex mirror."

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_3_adj"
	val[]: "@@adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_3_adj_img@@<br>Convex mirrors provide a wider field of view, allowing you to see more of what is going on beside you.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_selectfcs@@ to continue. </font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_4_adj"
	val[]: "Ideally, you should see both the car and truck parked to the side while having a very small portion of your own truck still visible."

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_4_adj_big"
	val[]: "Once you are satisfied with the mirror adjustment, switch to the passenger's side convex mirror."

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_4_adj_moved"
	val[]: "Again, you should see both the car and truck parked to the side while still having a small portion of your own truck visible."

	key[]: "adj_tut_set_mirrors_t1_4_adj_moved_big"
	val[]: "Once you are satisfied with the mirror adjustment, press @@imv_nrm_back@@ to close the mirror settings."

	key[]: "adj_tut_back_adj"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_back@@ to return to the configuration menu. </font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_close_adj"
	val[]: "Excellent, with your seat and mirrors set to your liking, you are now one step closer to hitting the road!<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Close the configuration menu using @@imv_nrm_back@@. </font>"

	key[]: "adj_tut_open_con"
	val[]: "Take one more look around to ensure that you're satisfied with your view from the cab and that the mirrors provide you with a good view of what's happening around the truck.<br><br>If something doesn't suit you, you can adjust the mirrors again in '@@adjust_link_t@@' configuration menu. <br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_activate@@ to end the first scenario.</font> @@aca_goal_tip@@ To show or hide on-screen mirrors, you can go to '@@adjust_link_t@@' — '@@adj_ui_mirrors@@' in the pause menu. On-screen mirrors make it easier to view your passenger's side."
#@}

# Book 1 Scenario 1_02 - strings not needing translation
#!{
	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_cam_top"
	val[]: "@@o_im_freecam@@"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_cam_cabin"
	val[]: "@@o_im_topcam@@"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_cam_window"
	val[]: "@@o_im_uppercam@@"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_cam_interior"
	val[]: "@@o_im_wincam@@"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_end"
	val[]: "@@o_im_insidecam@@"
#!}


#+ Book 1 Scenario 1_02
#@{

#### 1_02 common

	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_02_title"
	val[]: "Camera Controls"

	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_02_desc"
	val[]: "In this scenario, we'll learn about the various types of cameras available to you and how they can help you to control and manoeuvre the truck."

#### 1_02 goal

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_seat"
	val[]: "Seating Position"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_look_back"
	val[]: "View to the Rear"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_mirrors"
	val[]: "Mirror Check"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_cam_behind"
	val[]: "Switch to External Camera"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_02_look_around"
	val[]: "Look Around the Truck"


#### 1_02 msg - intro text

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cutscene1"
	val[]: "In this scenario, we'll go through the different cameras<br>that are available to use."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cutscene2"
	val[]: "There are seven cameras to choose from in total, we'll go through<br> a few of them now and explain their intended functions."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cutscene3"
	val[]: "The various cameras and their different angles can help you when manoeuvring in tight places."


#### 1_02 Driving Instructions

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_seat"
	val[]: "Looking where you are going is the core foundation to safe and professional driving. If the current seating position does not suit you, you can change it in '@@adjust_link_t@@' (Access it via pause menu).<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Confirm when you are ready with @@imv_nrm_activate@@. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_look_back"
	val[]: "When reversing, your mirrors don't always offer a clear view. It may be necessary to look out the window behind you to get a better view.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Turn your camera all the way to the driver's side to look outside the window towards the rear of the trailer.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ You have to be inside the vehicle."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_mirrors"
	val[]: "Use this view to check on the trailer during reversing manoeuvres with a trailer. It's always better to reverse to the driver's side so that you can utilize this view. When reversing to the passenger side, you have a much more limited view of what is going on behind you.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Look towards the passenger's side. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cam_behind"
	val[]: "This is why it is usually not recommended to reverse towards the passenger's side; you can see that visibility is quite limited. Luckily, there are seven exterior cameras available to you as well. <br><br>The button @@imv_nrm_camcycle@@ can be used to switch to the next camera in sequence. After cycling through all seven cameras, you'll return to the beginning of the cycle. <br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_camcycle@@ to switch to the next camera. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_look_around"
	val[]: "The external camera provides the best perspective on what is happening around the truck.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Look around the truck.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cam_top"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Pressing @@imv_nrm_camcycle@@ again, you can switch to the next camera. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cam_cabin"
	val[]: "The top-down view provides an excellent overview of the situation around the truck, significantly simplifying parking and driving in tight spaces.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_camcycle@@ to switch to the next camera.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cam_window"
	val[]: "The roof camera provides a clear view of the road far in front of the truck without much obstruction.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_camcycle@@ to switch to the final camera we will look at for now.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_cam_interior"
	val[]: "The rear view is a shortcut to the view you obtained earlier by turning the interior camera. As we discussed, it's helpful when reversing or parking.<br><br>In the game, we have more cameras that you can try by repeatedly pressing @@imv_nrm_camcycle@@.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_cam1@@ to return to the interior.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_02_end"
	val[]: "For an authentic driving school experience, we recommend staying with the 'Interior Camera' view as you go through each of the scenarios.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_activate@@ to confirm and end the scenario.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ You can use the @@o_im_cam_zoom@@ feature for a better view of your surroundings. It's especially helpful when looking through the mirrors. Check the Options Screen - '@@options_bindings_screen@@' - to see and/or change corresponding controls."

#@}

#+ Book 1 Scenario 1_03
#@{

#### 1_03 common
	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_03_title"
	val[]: "First Drive"

	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_03_desc"
	val[]: "In this scenario, we'll learn how to prepare the truck to be driven, and then drive it forwards for the first time."

#### 1_03 goal

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_electrics"
	val[]: "Turning on the Ignition"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_start"
	val[]: "Starting the Engine"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_look_mirror"
	val[]: "Checking Surroundings"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_brake"
	val[]: "Applying Service Brake"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_gear"
	val[]: "Shifting into Gear"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_park_br_off"
	val[]: "Releasing the Parking Brake"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_forward"
	val[]: "Driving Forwards"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_stop"
	val[]: "Stopping"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_park_br_on"
	val[]: "Applying the Parking Brake"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_gear_n"
	val[]: "Shifting into Neutral"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_03_end"
	val[]: "Turning off the Engine"

#### 1_03 msg - intro text

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_cutscene1"
	val[]: "For your first few drives, we'll be using the tractor unit only.<br>A truck is referred to as a tractor when it doesn't have a cargo body of its own, and instead relies on the use of a trailer to transport goods and materials."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_cutscene2"
	val[]: "Tractors are common because they allow for greater versatility: they can drop an empty trailer and pick up a loaded one without having to wait, or switch to a different kind of trailer entirely."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_cutscene3"
	val[]: "For your first drive, your task will be to drive forward and stop after the dashed line.<br>Start the engine, follow the instructions to get the truck ready to move. Once prepared, drive straight ahead."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_cutscene4"
	val[]: "Drive past the dashed line, stop, shut down the engine, and secure the truck."

#### 1_03 Driving Instructions

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_electrics"
	val[]: "For the next step in your training, you'll move the truck for the first time.<br><br>Of course, without the engine running it won't work, so first you'll need to turn on the ignition.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press $input engineelect$ to turn on the ignition.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ In the Career, by default, the engine is turned on together with electricity automatically. For the Career, you can adjust this behaviour in the Options Screen - 'Gameplay' - @@auto_engine_start@@."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_start"
	val[]: "The ignition activates the truck's electronics. You may have noticed warning lamps flash on the dashboard - that is normal. If they remain on once the engine is started, then that likely signals a problem with the truck. The exception is the parking brake lamp, which will turn off when we release the parking brakes.<br><br>Luckily, this truck is in good condition and we are ready to proceed.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_engine@@ to start the engine. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_look_mirror"
	val[]: "Now that the engine is started, it's crucial to check your surroundings before starting any movement.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Look around the truck and at your driver's and passenger's side mirrors to confirm that the area surrounding the truck is clear.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ You have to be inside the vehicle."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_brake"
	val[]: "It may seem obvious, but you should know how to stop before starting any movement.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Activate the service brake using $input backward$. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_arcade"
	val[]: "Next, you'll learn how to change your direction of travel.<br><br>With a simplified automatic transmission, there's no need to shift gears, everything is done automatically for you.<font face=/font/big_bold.font><br><br>Use $input forward$ to activate a forward gear. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_automatic"
	val[]: "Next, you'll learn how to change your direction of travel.<br><br>The realistic automatic transmission allows you to shift between Drive, Neutral and Reverse just like real automatic transmissions.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_gearup@@ to activate a forward gear. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_manual"
	val[]: "Next, you'll learn how to change your direction of travel.<br><br>The sequential transmission allows for stepped shifting, just like real sequential transmissions.<br><br>In the same way as you engage a forward gear, while accelerating you will need to shift to higher gears.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_gearup@@  to engage first gear.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_direct"
	val[]: "Next, you'll learn how to change your direction of travel.<br><br>With the gear stick and clutch, you'll experience the same feeling of physically shifting gears as with a real manual transmission.<br><br>Fully press down the clutch and the service brake. <font face=/font/big_bold.font>Use the gear stick to engage first gear. <color value=@@clr_txt@@>Keep the clutch and the service brake fully depressed.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_park_br_off"
	val[]: "To start moving, you must first release the parking brake.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Use @@imv_nrm_parkingbrake@@ to release the parking brake.</font> @@aca_goal_tip@@ In the Career, the parking brake is initially disabled. You can adjust this behaviour in the Options Screen - 'Gameplay' - @@auto_park_brake@@."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_forward_arcade"
	val[]: "Now the truck is ready to move forwards. Start moving and cross the dashed line.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Initiate movement by using the accelerator: $input forward$ </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_forward_automatic"
	val[]: "Now the truck is ready to move forwards. Start moving and cross the dashed line.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Initiate movement by using the accelerator: $input forward$ </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_forward_manual"
	val[]: "Now the truck is ready to move forwards. Start moving and cross the dashed line.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Initiate movement by using the accelerator: $input forward$ </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_forward_direct"
	val[]: "Now the truck is ready to move forwards. Start moving and cross the dashed line.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Release the service brake, gradually release the clutch to engage it while simultaneously using the accelerator to keep your RPM up so the truck doesn't stall. Once the clutch is fully released you can accelerate and shift as necessary. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_stop_arcade"
	val[]: "Use the service brake to stop.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Use $input backward$ to stop the truck. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_stop_automatic"
	val[]: "Use the service brake to stop.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Use $input backward$ to stop the truck. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_stop_manual"
	val[]: "Use the service brake to stop.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Use $input backward$ to stop the truck. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_stop_direct"
	val[]: "When it's time to stop, depress the clutch fully <font face=/font/big_bold.font>and then stop the truck using the service brake.<color value=@@clr_txt@@> Shift to neutral using the gear stick, and then you may release the clutch. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_park_br_on"
	val[]: "Now, secure the truck. The parking brake ensures the truck won't move unintentionally after you've parked.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Use @@imv_nrm_parkingbrake@@ to activate the parking brake.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_n_arcade"
	val[]: "With a simplified automatic transmission, there's no need to shift gears, everything is done automatically for you.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_activate@@ to confirm. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_n_automatic"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Shift into neutral by pressing @@imv_nrm_geardown@@. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_n_manual"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Shift into neutral by pressing @@imv_nrm_geardown@@. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_gear_n_direct"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Shift the gear stick into neutral, then release the clutch. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_03_end"
	val[]: "You now know how to get the truck moving and how to bring it to a stop safely.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press $input engineelect$ to turn the engine off. </font>"
#@}

#+ Book 1 Scenario 1_04
#@{

#### 1_04 common
	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_04_title"
	val[]: "Reversing"

	key[]: "aca_scenario_book1_1_04_desc"
	val[]: "In this scenario, we'll try reversing for the first time. We'll also talk about how to utilize your mirrors to see behind you, what to watch for, and how to prepare for reverse movement."

#### 1_04 goal

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_start"
	val[]: "Starting the Engine"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_look_mirror"
	val[]: "Checking Passenger's Side Mirror"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_look_back"
	val[]: "Checking Driver's Side Mirror"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_gear_r"
	val[]: "Shifting into Gear"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_park_br_off"
	val[]: "Releasing the Parking Brake"

#!{
	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_backward"
	val[]: "@@aca_scenario_book1_1_04_title@@"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_stop"
	val[]: "@@aca_goal_book1_1_03_stop@@"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_park_br_on"
	val[]: "@@aca_goal_book1_1_03_park_br_on@@"

#!}


	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_gear_n"
	val[]: "Shifting into Neutral"

	key[]: "aca_goal_book1_1_04_end"
	val[]: "Turning off the Engine"

#### 1_04 msg - intro text

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_cutscene1"
	val[]: "For this drive, we'll be reversing in a straight line. You'll have to reverse past the dashed line and stop there."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_cutscene2"
	val[]: "When reversing the truck, it is essential to look around constantly, observe all the mirrors, and ensure that the space around and behind you is clear."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_cutscene3"
	val[]: "Start the engine, shift to reverse, and begin moving."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_cutscene4"
	val[]: "Reverse past the dashed line, stop, shut down the engine, and secure the truck."

#### 1_04 Driving Instructions

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_start"
	val[]: "Prepare the truck to be driven as you learned in the previous scenario.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>When you're ready, turn on the engine. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_look_mirror"
	val[]: "Check your mirrors to ensure the area around you is clear. If you are unsatisfied with their positions, you can adjust them in '@@adjust_link_t@@'.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Look at your passenger's side mirror.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ You have to be inside the vehicle."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_look_back"
	val[]: "You'll be moving past the broken line. The lane is clear now, but during regular driving, it's essential to constantly monitor your surroundings by looking around and using the mirrors.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Check your driver's side mirror.</font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_r_arcade"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Use $input backward$ to engage reverse gear. </font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ When reversing, the backup alarm automatically activates on most trucks. You can turn it off in the Options Screen - 'Audio' - @@sound_of_reverse@@."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_r_automatic"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_geardown@@ to shift into reverse. </font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ When reversing, the backup alarm automatically activates on most trucks. You can turn it off in the Options Screen - 'Audio' - @@sound_of_reverse@@."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_r_manual"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_geardown@@ to shift into reverse. </font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ When reversing, the backup alarm automatically activates on most trucks. You can turn it off in the Options Screen - 'Audio' - @@sound_of_reverse@@."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_r_direct"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Depress the clutch fully and move your gear stick into reverse. </font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ When reversing, the backup alarm automatically activates on most trucks. You can turn it off in the Options Screen - 'Audio' - @@sound_of_reverse@@."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_park_br_off"
	val[]: "You now have reverse gear engaged.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Release the parking brake using @@imv_nrm_parkingbrake@@. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_backward_arcade"
	val[]: "Begin moving by using $input backward$.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Reverse past the dashed line. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_backward_automatic"
	val[]: "Begin moving by using the accelerator: $input forward$.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Reverse past the dashed line. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_backward_manual"
	val[]: "Begin moving by using the accelerator: $input forward$.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Reverse past the dashed line. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_backward_direct"
	val[]: "Release the clutch slowly, while maintaining the engine's RPM by using the accelerator. <br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Reverse past the dashed line. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_stop_arcade"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Stop the truck using your service brake: $input forward$ </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_stop_automatic"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Stop the truck using your service brake: $input backward$ </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_stop_manual"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Stop the truck using your service brake: $input backward$ </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_stop_direct"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Depress the clutch fully and then stop the truck using your service brakes. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_park_br_on"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Activate the parking brake using @@imv_nrm_parkingbrake@@. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_n_arcade"
	val[]: "With a simplified automatic transmission, there's no need to shift gears as everything is done automatically for you, unlike in reality.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Press @@imv_nrm_activate@@ to confirm. </font>"

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_n_automatic"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Shift into neutral by pressing @@imv_nrm_gearup@@.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@ Modern trucks will automatically shift to neutral when the parking brake is applied. However, it is a good habit to always do it yourself. In the following scenarios, we will not require this step."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_n_manual"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Shift into neutral by pressing @@imv_nrm_gearup@@.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@  Modern trucks will automatically shift to neutral when the parking brake is applied. However, it is a good habit to always do it yourself. In the following scenarios, we will not require this step."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_gear_n_direct"
	val[]: "<font face=/font/big_bold.font>Shift the gear stick into neutral, then release the clutch.</font>@@aca_goal_tip@@  Modern trucks will automatically shift to neutral when the parking brake is applied. However, it is a good habit to always do it yourself. In the following scenarios, we will not require this step."

	key[]: "aca_msg_book1_1_04_end"
	val[]: "Remember to always be aware of your surroundings as you reverse, especially in busy areas with lots of traffic.<br><br><font face=/font/big_bold.font>Shut down the engine by pressing $input engineelect$. </font>"
#@}

